# ${slug_title} AI-native engineering

Planning, design, or implementation in this repo: read and follow
`/10x-engineer` then `/${adapter}` (path remaps). One skill per turn.
Do not invent a workflow. Do not restate either skill's tables here.

${jira_line}

If `.cursor/rules/${slug}-project.mdc` exists, read it for project conventions.
`packs`, `board`, `default_branch`, `decision_policy`, and `tracker` live in `${root}/.ai-native.yml`.

If `${root}/INDEX.md` exists, read it. Honor `layout`, `current`,
`current_feature`, and path keys (`features_dir`, `sprint_planning_dir`,
`sprints_dir`, `tickets_dir`). Then read that folder INDEX.
Honor `phase`, `skill`, and `ticket`. Then read that named skill's `SKILL.md`.

If `${root}/TOOLS.md` exists, use those tools. Skip MCPs that are missing.
Graft first for file/symbol discovery (`ask`, `callers`, `skeleton`,
`map`) before grep or reading a whole file.

Lookup: `${root}/README.md` → `TOOLS.md` → INDEX (via `layout`) → one
ticket `INDEX.md` (under `features/<feature>/tickets/` when `layout` is
`features`, otherwise `planning/tickets/`) then that ticket's `plan.md`.
Preliminary decisions can change until the feature merges. Decisions that
apply are inlined in `plan.md`. Next work from `progress.md`. Mutate
`${root}/` per `README.md`. Plan chat writes spec + `plan.md`; implement
executes and sets `in_review`; `/code-review` reports only. `done` only
after merge to `${default_branch}`. After that merge, `ship-ticket` if `board`
is markdown. Do not promote feature decisions from a ticket close. INDEX is not the board.

No ticket AC in this rule. No copy of skill text. ${memory_commit}
`graft/` is gitignored; `.cursorignore` re-includes it for Agent Glob/Grep.
